=head1 DESCRIPTION

This processor takes a list of objects that contain key fields, and
converts them into a map of target keys.

For more information about this processor including examples, see
listToMap
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CloudWatch-Logs-Transformation-Processors.html#CloudWatch-Logs-Transformation-listToMap)
in the I<CloudWatch Logs User Guide>.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 Flatten => Bool

A Boolean value to indicate whether the list will be flattened into
single items. Specify C<true> to flatten the list. The default is
C<false>


=head2 FlattenedElement => Str

If you set C<flatten> to C<true>, use C<flattenedElement> to specify
which element, C<first> or C<last>, to keep.

You must specify this parameter if C<flatten> is C<true>


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Key => Str

The key of the field to be extracted as keys in the generated map


=head2 B<REQUIRED> Source => Str

The key in the log event that has a list of objects that will be
converted to a map.


=head2 Target => Str

The key of the field that will hold the generated map


=head2 ValueKey => Str

If this is specified, the values that you specify in this parameter
will be extracted from the C<source> objects and put into the values of
the generated map. Otherwise, original objects in the source list will
be put into the values of the generated map.



